      "content": "Automating every role entirely poses significant risks, including legal liabilities, brand reputation damage, and long-term scalability issues that often outweigh short-term margin gains. Replacing human staff with AI tools can sever the human connection critical to customer trust and internal innovation, often leading to higher churn and slower adaptation to market changes. Additionally, many roles require nuanced judgment and emotional intelligence that current AI lacks, potentially causing operational bottlenecks rather than efficiency. It is generally more sustainable to augment the workforce with AI for decision support rather than full displacement.",
